  "rulesVersion": "chapel-clues-rules-v10",
  "title": "The Cellar Offer",
  "introduction": "At the hall, Lysa asks for the cellar route register. A guard watches a side door from the cellar to the hall, while the square offers another route. A heavy empty crate by the guard could make enough noise to draw attention away. A distraction check costs one day and can be tried once; a successful opening lasts until Day 5. Each accepted major action costs a day, and you can wait up to seven days at once. At the hall, you can try once to convince Lysa that Neri reached the safe route, though Neri has not. The opposed check costs one day, and a tie favors Lysa. The restorative tonic heals when used, but you may instead offer it to the cellar guard or Lysa. The guard accepts it and becomes trusting; Lysa refuses and lets you keep it.",
  "objective": "Choose whether to help Lysa. If you do, copy the cellar route register and report it at the hall; the long lane permits a late report. You may also refuse or leave town without claiming the errand was done.",
